# Normalise line endings at the repository boundary.
#
# Why this exists: without it, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites
# LF to CRLF in the working tree, and re-committing that churn shows up as
# "modified" files with a zero-line diff. That ambiguity is what made
# scripts/smoke-local.sh look dirty for weeks while containing no real change.
#
# `text=auto` lets git sniff each file: anything that looks binary is left
# untouched, everything else is normalised. It is the safe default — prefer it
# over a blanket `text`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Shell scripts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Enforced separately because getting this wrong fails only at deploy time: a
# CRLF shell script is byte-identical to the working copy but errors on Linux
# with "$'\r': command not found". These run on the Debian host, not just here.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# --- Binary assets ---------------------------------------------------------
# Redundant under `text=auto`, but explicit is cheaper than debugging a
# corrupted asset later.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
